    "blocks": [
      {
        "id": "p1",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "What do you see when you look up at the sky? If you do this on a nice day, you may be able to see some beautiful clouds. You may even get "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "inspired",
            "ref": "v-inspire"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " on occasion to take photos of such clouds."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p2",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Chris Judge, an Irish artist, goes a step further. He turns these clouds into playful cartoon characters. The 46-year-old artist first began to create cloud art out of "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "boredom",
            "ref": "v-boredom"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ". One day, some pink clouds "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "caught his eye",
            "ref": "v-catch-eye"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ". Those clouds looked like a monkey and a bear. The man took photos of them and drew some very simple pencil lines on top of these photos. He then shared his creations on social media. To his surprise, people liked them very much. Since then, he has been making one every day."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p3",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Judge imagines clouds as many different characters. Sometimes the shapes are easy to see, and other times he needs to use his "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "imagination",
            "ref": "v-imagination"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ". He now often finds faces in unexpected places. But no matter what, the artist doesn’t want his "
          },
          {
            "t": "underline",
            "v": "doodles"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " to end up covering up too much of the cloud. “So I try to draw as few lines as possible,” he said."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p4",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "The artist has a book coming out next year called "
          },
          {
            "t": "em",
            "v": "Cloud Babies"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ". After hearing his story, would you like to try your hand at making your own cloud art?"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "i1",
        "type": "imageRef",
        "image": "img1"
      }
    ]
  },
